  "title": "Inpatient delivery",
  "description": "Inpatient delivery is a hospitalization that covers your delivery at the hospital, where your baby is born and you receive comprehensive labor and delivery care. You'll be admitted when labor begins or when your doctor schedules your delivery. Your medical team monitors you and your baby throughout labor, manages pain as needed, and assists with delivery. After delivery, you'll stay in the hospital for recovery and to ensure both you and your baby are healthy. This type of delivery can occur various ways, including vaginal delivery (including VBAC) or cesarean section, and the cost may vary depending on the method of delivery.",
